The plate is square and roughly 26 cm across. It holds about 10 chunks of honeydew melon or a similar green fruit, each roughly 3 cm across. That adds up to about 100 g of fruit, since each chunk is around 10 g.

Honeydew is about 36 kcal per 100 g, so 100 g comes to roughly 36 kcal. I'll allow a little extra in case the fruit is heavier than I estimated, which gives about 40 kcal for around 110 g.

